    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Casey Kennedy are delighted to present this fine detached bungalow situated in this most convenient location close to the junction of Avondale Road and Cluney Grove and within walking distance of Killiney Shopping Centre and a host of local amenities. Built in 1950`s this property boasts spacious accommodation of approximately 183 sq.m (1,970 sq.ft) with a very private west facing garden to the rear. It offers excellent potential to extend or develop subject to the relevant planning permission. The accommodation which is bright and airy briefly comprises of a welcoming entrance hall opening through to a large living room positioned at the front, a spacious modern kitchen/dining room, a family/TV room, 4/5 bedrooms, one with an en-suite bathroom and a family bathroom. The property is well set back from the road and offers off street car parking for 3 cars. To the rear of the property there is a large west facing private, mature garden with mature trees, shrubs, fruit trees and lawn. \n\nAvondale Road is a mature highly regarded residential road within close proximity of a wide range of conveniences. The property is located just a short walk from every imaginable amenity and facility in Dalkey, Killiney and Dun Laoghaire with their specialist and boutique shops, banks, delicatessens, shopping centres, cafes and some of South County Dublin`s finest restaurants. Public transport is excellent with Glenageary DART Station just a short walk away and numerous bus routes to include the 59 bus to Dun Laoghaire along with the Aircoach at Killiney Castle providing ease of access to the city centre and the Airport. Local shopping is available just up the road at Killiney Shopping Centre. There are a host of excellent primary and secondary schools close by to include Glenageary & Killiney National School, Dalkey School Project, Rathdown, Castle Park, St. Joseph`s of Cluny, Harold National School, Gaelscoil Phadraig and Loreto Abbey Dalkey. \n\nThere is also a wide range of sporting and recreational amenities in the immediate area including Killiney Golf Club just up the road and tennis clubs as well as the hugely popular sailing and marine activities at the yacht clubs and marina in Dun Laoghaire Harbour. The walks over Dalkey and Killiney hill and along the seafront are particularly popular and offer stunning views. \n\nNo.102 Avondale Road represents a rare opportunity to acquire a well- presented five bedroom bungalow with an exceptional west-facing garden, in one of South Dublin`s most sought-after coastal neighbourhoods.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway - 3.02m (9'11\") x 2.36m (7'9\")\n\nLivingroom - 6.14m (20'2\") x 5.54m (18'2\")\nBright spacious reception room with open fireplace with gas fire\n\nKitchen - 4.21m (13'10\") x 4.12m (13'6\")\nExtensive fitted floor and wall units, Built in double oven, microwave and ceramic hob, dishwasher and fridge freezer, tiled floor and walls, door to\n\nUtility Room - 2.7m (8'10\") x 1.5m (4'11\")\nPlumbed for washing machine, floor and wall units, door to rear garden and patio\n\nFamily/TV Room - 5.45m (17'11\") x 2.68m (8'10\")\nLaminate wooden flooring\n\nBedroom 2/Playroom - 3.2m (10'6\") x 2.55m (8'4\")\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.8m (12'6\") x 3.2m (10'6\")\nWooden floor\n\nBedroom 4 - 4.08m (13'5\") x 3.31m (10'10\")\nBuilt in wardrobe , wooden floor.\n\nFamily Bathroom - 2.77m (9'1\") x 1.85m (6'1\")\nElectric Shower, w.c., w.h.b., heated towel rail, tiled floor and walls.\n\nUpstairs\nSpiral staircase to\n\nBedroom 1 (Master) - 4.51m (14'10\") x 3.95m (13'0\")\nBuilt in sliderobe\n\nEnsuite Bathroom - 3.08m (10'1\") x 2.63m (8'8\")\nBath, separate shower, w.c., bidet and wash hand basin, tiled walls and laminate wooden flooring.\n\nLanding - 2.6m (8'6\") x 1.95m (6'5\")\nAdditional storage\n\nBedroom 5/Dressing room - 3.4m (11'2\") x 3.1m (10'2\")\n\nAttic Room - 6.1m (20'0\") x 5.5m (18'1\")\nSpacious Attic room with high ceiling and offers potential to convert and extend the living accommodation subject to PP\n\nOutside\nRear Garden:\n16.3m x 12.30m\nPrivate, mature, well maintained, west facing with mature trees, shrubs, lawn, outside sheds and a large paved patio.\nOff street parking for 3 cars to the front\n\n\nNotice\nIntending purchasers must satisfy themselves as to the accuracy\nof all information and measurements in this listing. Any particulars\nprovided are for guidance only and do not constitute a contract or a part of\none. We do not accept responsibility for any loss or damage arising from\nreliance on this information. Purchasers should seek independent legal and\nprofessional advice."
